Well that sucks. And you seem to know the rules. Spellcasters really really
need to take advantage of the protection game that the priests offer. You can
pay to get your armor class lowered 8 to 10 AC and it costs nothing to carry
or wear. I didn't used to do it because I thought that you had to only chat
to coaligned priests. But you can take the blessing from any priest(ess) 
without penalty. It really now defines what the purpose of money is.

Note that the cost is level dependant. Check out this page if you want all
the gory details:

http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/prst-343.txt

So even in your situation you could have bought yourself to negative protection
from the minetown preist.

Also you can manage metal armor too. As a wizard I always wear orcish helms,
hard hats (even better with -2 to AC) and hard shoes. They of course have a
cumulative effect. But walking around the dungeon it's critical to lower your
AC, as a high AC is the fastest way to get killed.

You can go whole hog and become a Warrior Wizard. Go ahead and armor up with
whatever you can find, grab your staff, and whack away. Banded (or mithril
coats) , hard hat, hard shoes, CoMR, and priest(ess) protection can get you
in the negative teens even without ?oEA (which of course you don't even want
to use unless they are blessed. Banded is the best because of its AC reduction
(-6) to weight (90) ratio. Much better than anything around it. Only splint
is in the ballpark. The dragon mail is the absolute best because of AC 
reduction (-9) weight (40) and the fact that it isn't metal so it doesn't 
affect spellcasting.

