So get it. It's more important to survive in the game than it is to cast
spells. Also wearing metal doesn't permanently affect your casting chances.
If you really really need to cast a spell you can always take it off.

Later in the game, items such as a enchanted Helm of Brilliance, or a Robe
can improve your spellcasting chances even if you are wearing metal.
Also once you get poly/polycontrol you can possible even eat rings of 
protection.

But in the early game the minetown priest is your best friend.

And a friendly side note, if you come across a wand of wishing early in the
game and wish yourself up a Archon for a pet, don't bring him to minetown
until after you've gotten all your protection. He'll kill the shopkeepers,
guards, and priests on the level. Otherwise a really really great pet.
But in armoring up, don't even think about it until you've gotten at least
your SDSM, 

