No. Simply armor up with what you have. In the early game the only thing you
don't want to personally be whacking are nymphs.

Strong pets are really really helpful. A kitty at level nine can destroy
anything the dungeon will generate if you are level 2 or three. You can pray
to satisfy hunger, so you should let your kitty (and get another or a doggy
when they are generated) kill and eat everything in sight in the early game.
Builds them up, and keeps your costs to the priests down. However the same
argument about the Archon (great pet! WOW!) applies here too. Don't bring them
into minetown because they'll try to kill all the guards.

My last game was a healer. Like you I finally got in trouble when I leveled
up and ran into a mumak in minetown. I had to dogs (Doggy and Scoobie) that
were both level 9. Healers can really treat their pets right because the
stethoscope can tell you the health of the pet, and you can heal them by
spell. They were taking out absolutely everything in sight. And yes, they 
killed and ate all the guards.
